+### [Explicit Mesh and Surface Reconstruction](18458-explicit-mesh-and-surface-reconstruction.md)
+This family encompasses methods that convert implicit neural radiance fields (NeRFs) or signed distance fields (SDFs) into explicit polygonal mesh representations or duplex surface structures [Explicit Mesh and Surface Reconstruction](18458-explicit-mesh-and-surface-reconstruction.md). It solves the problem of high computational cost and lack of explicit geometric topology in volumetric NeRFs by replacing dense ray sampling with surface intersections or deformable anchor grids. It differs from sibling methods like [I2-SDF](18170-i2-sdf.md) and [SDF-based Volume Rendering with Laplacian CDF](18174-sdf-based-volume-rendering-with-laplacian-cdf.md) by prioritizing explicit mesh extraction or duplex surface approximation for real-time rendering, rather than optimizing a continuous SDF field for volume rendering integration [Explicit Mesh and Surface Reconstruction](18458-explicit-mesh-and-surface-reconstruction.md).
+
+### [NeuralUDF](20281-neuraludf.md)
+NeuralUDF is a method for multi-view surface reconstruction that uses Unsigned Distance Fields (UDF) and volume rendering to recover surfaces with arbitrary topologies, including open surfaces, without requiring 3D ground truth shapes [NeuralUDF](20281-neuraludf.md). Unlike SDF-based methods that are limited to closed shapes, NeuralUDF avoids the sign ambiguity of SDFs by modeling the distance to the nearest surface as a strictly positive value, using probabilistic models to locate surface intersections and enforce color consistency [NeuralUDF](20281-neuraludf.md).
+
+### [IDR (Implicit Differentiable Renderer)](20341-idr-implicit-differentiable-renderer.md)
+IDR is a method for learning a neural Signed Distance Function (SDF) and camera parameters simultaneously from uncalibrated images [IDR (Implicit Differentiable Renderer)](20341-idr-implicit-differentiable-renderer.md). It disentangles geometry and appearance by combining a DVR-like implicit surface MLP with a NeRF-like view-dependent branch [IDR (Implicit Differentiable Renderer)](20341-idr-implicit-differentiable-renderer.md). Unlike standard NeRF which models volume density, IDR represents geometry as the zero-level set of an MLP and uses a neural renderer to approximate light reflection [IDR (Implicit Differentiable Renderer)](20341-idr-implicit-differentiable-renderer.md).
+
+### SDF-based NeRF
+- [S1, unofficial] Uses an SDF representation instead of volume densities to reconstruct scenes from RGB-D data, converting sdf values to densities for the NeRF formulation.
+
+### NeuS (Neural Implicit Surface)
+- [S2] A scene representation using two neural implicit functions encoded by MLPs to model accurate surface geometry and appearance from unconstrained Internet photos with varying lighting.
+- [S2] $d = \text{MLP}_{\text{SDF}}(\mathbf{x})$, where $\mathbf{x}$ is a point in $\mathbb{R}^3$. $d$ approximates the signed distance to the true surface $S$.
 
